, who won two medals each in gold and silver and one in bronze. The only other nation to win an event was Czechoslovakia, who took the double sculls with a surprise victory from " [:a {:href "/athletes/40009"} "Václav Kozák"] " and " [:a {:href "/athletes/40064"} "Pavel Schmidt"] "."] "\n\n" [:p {} "By entering " [:a {:href "/athletes/39270"} "Estuardo Masías"] " and " [:a {:href "/athletes/39274"} "Víctor Puente"] " into the double sculls, Peru made its début in Olympic rowing in Rome. The United Arab Republic, formed by a merger of Egypt and Syria in 1958, also took part for the first time as a new entity, although Egypt had competed separately in several previous editions and all of the UAR’s rowers in the coxed eights were Egyptian by birth. Nonetheless, the total number of participating nations hit 33, tying the record set in 1952."] "\n\n"] "\n\n" [:h2 {} "Events"] "\n" [:table {:class "table table-striped"} "\n" [:thead {} "\n" [:tr {} "\n" [:th {} "Event"] "\n" [:th {} "Status"] "\n" [:th {} "Date"] "\n" [:th {} "Participants"] "\n" [:th {} "NOCs"] "\n"] "\n"] "\n" [:tbody {} [:tr {} "\n" [:td {} [:a {:href "/results/158312"} "Single Sculls, Men"]] "\n" [:td {} "Olympic"] "\n" [:td {} "30 August –  3 September 1960"] "\n" [:td {} "13"] "\n" [:td {} "13"] "\n"] "\n" [:tr {} "\n" [:td {} [:a {:href "/results/158322"} "Double Sculls, Men"]] "\n" [:td {} "Olympic"] "\n" [:td {} "31 August –  3 September 1960"] "\n" [:td {} "32"] "\n" [:td {} "16"] "\n"] "\n" [:tr {} "\n" [:td {} [:a {:href "/results/158332"} "Coxless Pairs, Men"]] "\n" [:td {} "Olympic"] "\n" [:td {} "30 August –  3 September 1960"] "\n" [:td {} "36"] "\n" [:td {} "18"] "\n"] "\n" [:tr {} "\n" [:td {} [:a {:href "/results/158347"} "Coxed Pairs, Men"]] "\n" [:td {} "Olympic"] "\n" [:td {} "31 August –  3 September 1960"] "\n" [:td {} "54"] "\n" [:td {} "18"] "\n"] "\n" [:tr {} "\n" [:td {} [:a {:href "/results/158357"} "Coxless Fours, Men"]] "\n" [:td {} "Olympic"] "\n" [:td {} "31 August –  3 Se